    <Folder>
      <name>Public Engagement</name>
    </Folder>
    <Folder>
      <name>Metro Line LRT</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Phase 1 - NAIT/Blatchford Market to Blatchford Gate </name>
        <description><![CDATA[After leaving NAIT/Blatchford Market Station, the train will travel to Blatchford Gate Station. Service will occur once ridership demand requires it.<br><br>Edmontonians in communities Northwest of City Centre share their vision of the Metro Line Northwest LRT Extension.<br><br>What We Heard: <br>https://www.edmonton.ca/documents/RoadsTraffic/MetroLineNWWhatWeHeardReportFall2017.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#line-0288D1-4000</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>
            -113.508602,53.566446,0
            -113.512416,53.571664,0
          </coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Complete - Blatchford Gate Station</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Blatchford Gate Station is complete, but not operational until transit service standards met.<br><br>What We Heard:<br>https://www.edmonton.ca/documents/RoadsTraffic/MetroLineNWWhatWeHeardReportFall2017.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#line-9C27B0-4875</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>
            -113.512974,53.581067,0
            -113.5128023,53.5779331,0
          </coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Phase 2 - Blatchford to Castle Downs</name>
        <description><![CDATA[There will be an elevated bridge crossing Yellowhead Trail and the CN Walker Yard. A bridge with a shared-use path provides a safe crossing for pedestrians and cyclists. <br><br>Edmontonians in communities Northwest of City Centre share their vision of the Metro Line Northwest LRT Extension.<br><br>What We Heard: <br>https://www.edmonton.ca/documents/RoadsTraffic/MetroLineNWWhatWeHeardReportFall2017.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#line-CE93D8-5000</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>
            -113.512974,53.581067,0
            -113.516482,53.585047,0
          </coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Phase 2 - Blatchford to Castle Downs</name>
        <description><![CDATA[The LRT will continue northwest towards 113A Street.Travelling at-grade through the 129 Avenue intersection and continuing north along the center of 113a Street. <br><br>The LRT will continue north, with an intersection at 130 Avenue. The LRT runs parallel with a proposed shared-use path for pedestrians and cyclists that will provide a connection from the Lauderdale off-leash area north to Castle Downs Park. <br><br>Edmontonians in communities Northwest of City Centre share their vision of the Metro Line Northwest LRT Extension.<br><br>What We Heard: <br>https://www.edmonton.ca/documents/RoadsTraffic/MetroLineNWWhatWeHeardReportFall2017.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#line-9C27B0-4000</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>
            -113.516482,53.585047,0
            -113.516428,53.592151,0
          </coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Phase 2 - Blatchford to Castle Downs</name>
        <description><![CDATA[The LRT continues north past Rosslyn Park. Streetside parking is provided in the southbound direction from 134 Avenue to 135 Avenue<br><br>Edmontonians in communities Northwest of City Centre share their vision of the Metro Line Northwest LRT Extension.<br><br>What We Heard: <br>https://www.edmonton.ca/documents/RoadsTraffic/MetroLineNWWhatWeHeardReportFall2017.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#line-9C27B0-4000</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>
            -113.516428,53.592151,0
            -113.516534,53.594917,0
            -113.516643,53.594979,0
            -113.516674,53.594999,0
            -113.516656,53.599596,0
          </coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Phase 2 - Blatchford to Castle Downs</name>
        <description><![CDATA[The 137 Avenue Station will be a trenched station where the LRT travels just below ground through an underpass. A trenched station will help mitigate east-west traffic impacts on 137 Avenue and allow pedestrians to access the station without having to cross the intersection. <br><br>Edmontonians in communities Northwest of City Centre share their vision of the Metro Line Northwest LRT Extension.<br><br>What We Heard: <br>https://www.edmonton.ca/documents/RoadsTraffic/MetroLineNWWhatWeHeardReportFall2017.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#line-9C27B0-4000</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>
            -113.516656,53.599596,0
            -113.516675,53.600515,0
            -113.516536,53.600712,0
            -113.516579,53.602011,0
          </coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Phase 2 - Blatchford to Castle Downs</name>
        <description><![CDATA[The LRT will continue north along the center of Castle Downs Road.<br><br>The LRT will travel below ground through an underpass at 139 Avenue and Castle Downs Road.<br><br>Edmontonians in communities Northwest of City Centre share their vision of the Metro Line Northwest LRT Extension.<br><br>What We Heard: <br>https://www.edmonton.ca/documents/RoadsTraffic/MetroLineNWWhatWeHeardReportFall2017.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#line-9C27B0-4000</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>
            -113.516579,53.602011,0
            -113.516729,53.602106,0
            -113.516729,53.607059,0
          </coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Phase 2 - Blatchford to Castle Downs</name>
        <description><![CDATA[The LRT will continue north along the center of Castle Downs Road past the Caernarvon and Griesbach neighbourhoods, with an intersection located at 152 Avenue/McCrae Avenue.<br><br>Edmontonians in communities Northwest of City Centre share their vision of the Metro Line Northwest LRT Extension.<br><br>What We Heard: <br>https://www.edmonton.ca/documents/RoadsTraffic/MetroLineNWWhatWeHeardReportFall2017.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#line-9C27B0-4000</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>
            -113.516729,53.607056,0
            -113.516707,53.613972,0
            -113.516906,53.614239,0
            -113.517483,53.614309,0
            -113.518987,53.614296,0
          </coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Phase 3 - Castle Downs to Campbell Road</name>
        <description><![CDATA[The LRT will continue west until it reaches the at-grade 137 Street Station. This station will service the neighbourhoods of Oxford and Carlton to the north, and Cumberland to the south.<br><br>Edmontonians in communities Northwest of City Centre share their vision of the Metro Line Northwest LRT Extension.<br><br>What We Heard: <br>https://www.edmonton.ca/documents/RoadsTraffic/MetroLineNWWhatWeHeardReportFall2017.pdf]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#line-9C27B0-4000</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>
            -113.519009,53.614322,0
            -113.5208,53.614354,0
            -113.52138,53.614296,0
            -113.523322,53.614669,0
            -113.524979,53.615235,0
